  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"67\" data-end=\"338\">The <strong data-start=\"71\" data-end=\"110\">ImmunoCAP Aspergillus fumigatus IgG</strong> test measures the level of <strong data-start=\"138\" data-end=\"156\">IgG antibodies</strong> specific to <em data-start=\"169\" data-end=\"192\">Aspergillus fumigatus</em>, a common environmental mold. Elevated IgG levels indicate <strong data-start=\"252\" data-end=\"297\">chronic or subacute exposure or infection</strong>, rather than an acute allergic reaction.</p>\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_16hzy_1\">\n<div class=\"_tableWrapper_16hzy_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"732\" data-end=\"1097\">\n<thead data-start=\"732\" data-end=\"847\">\n<tr data-start=\"732\" data-end=\"847\">\n<th data-start=\"732\" data-end=\"761\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"734\" data-end=\"744\">Result</strong></th>\n<th data-start=\"761\" data-end=\"847\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"763\" data-end=\"781\">Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody data-start=\"965\" data-end=\"1097\">\n<tr data-start=\"965\" data-end=\"1071\">\n<td data-start=\"965\" data-end=\"995\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"967\" data-end=\"990\">Elevated IgG Levels</strong></td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"995\" data-end=\"1071\">Suggests <strong data-start=\"1006\" data-end=\"1039\">chronic exposure or infection</strong> with <em data-start=\"1045\" data-end=\"1068\">Aspergillus fumigatus</em>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1097\">\n<td data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1097\" data-col-size=\"sm\">May support diagnosis of:</td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none\">\n<div class=\"absolute end-0 flex items-end\">&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<ul data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1566\">\n<li data-start=\"1098\" data-end=\"1141\">\n<p data-start=\"1100\" data-end=\"1141\"><strong data-start=\"1100\" data-end=\"1141\">Chronic pulmonary aspergillosis (CPA)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1142\" data-end=\"1160\">\n<p data-start=\"1144\" data-end=\"1160\"><strong data-start=\"1144\" data-end=\"1160\">Aspergilloma</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1161\" data-end=\"1566\">\n<p data-start=\"1163\" data-end=\"1566\"><strong data-start=\"1163\" data-end=\"1195\">Hypersensitivity pneumonitis</strong><br data-start=\"1195\" data-end=\"1198\">Should be interpreted in conjunction with <strong data-start=\"1240\" data-end=\"1286\">clinical findings, imaging, and other labs</strong> (e.g., total IgE, precipitins, cultures).&nbsp;<br><strong data-start=\"1333\" data-end=\"1361\">Normal or Low IgG Levels</strong> | Makes active <em data-start=\"1377\" data-end=\"1400\">Aspergillus fumigatus</em> infection <strong data-start=\"1411\" data-end=\"1426\">less likely</strong>, but does not entirely rule it out.<br data-start=\"1462\" data-end=\"1465\">Consider other markers (e.g., galactomannan, beta-D-glucan) or repeat testing if suspicion remains.&nbsp;</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1927\" data-end=\"1946\"><strong data-start=\"1931\" data-end=\"1946\">Limitations</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1947\" data-end=\"2115\">\n<li data-start=\"1947\" data-end=\"1999\">\n<p data-start=\"1949\" data-end=\"1999\">May cross-react with other <strong data-start=\"1976\" data-end=\"1999\">Aspergillus species</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2000\" data-end=\"2065\">\n<p data-start=\"2002\" data-end=\"2065\"><strong data-start=\"2002\" data-end=\"2049\">Not useful for acute invasive aspergillosis</strong> diagnosis alone</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2066\" data-end=\"2115\">\n<p data-start=\"2068\" data-end=\"2115\"><strong data-start=\"2068\" data-end=\"2094\">IgG levels may persist</strong> even after treatment</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
